{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A formatted credential near the runner’s output cutoff can leave its unredacted suffix in persisted output and model inputs."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A formatted multiline credential can appear in full in failure excerpts that are persisted or sent as feedback."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Overlapping credentials split across output chunks can expose the sensitive extension of the longer credential."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"Fields containing the common redaction marker are withheld in full, obscuring useful diagnostics."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"Generic API and event payloads are silently modified and may receive gate-specific metadata."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Serving artifacts can alter their contents, including removing literal escape bytes from a stored patch."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The inline review patch can omit literal escape sequences present in the actual source change."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"compat","trigger":"unusual","reason":"After rollback, an older release can misclassify a saved successful gate as a blocking confinement failure when its formatted output normalizes to the error phrase."}]}